# Line endings. A clone must look like the tree it was made from, byte for byte, and this
# repository mixes two conventions: most C++ sources, headers, JSON data and many documents are
# CRLF (Westwood's and the client's habit); the files listed below are LF. Nothing is converted
# on checkout or commit (`-text`), so core.autocrlf on a contributor's machine cannot change a
# blob. Keep each file's existing ending when you edit it (docs/builders.md, "Scripts and docs");
# tools/docs_check.py fails on a file that mixes the two.
#
# To add a new LF file, list it in the block below; anything not listed is stored as written
# (new C++ and docs files follow their neighbours: CRLF).
* -text

